# Intentionally empty of NEXT_PUBLIC_* values.
#
# Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the client bundle at build time. The Heroku
# slug is built once and promoted across apps, so anything inlined here would
# describe the app the slug was built in rather than the app serving the
# request -- which is how production came to list development's hydrophones.
#
# The per-environment values arrive at runtime instead:
#   - GraphQL and socket endpoints resolve same-origin in the browser, and from
#     GQL_ENDPOINT server-side. See src/graphql/client.ts and src/hooks/useSocket.ts.
#   - S3_BUCKET and GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID are injected per request by
#     /api/runtime-config. See src/utils/runtimeConfig.ts.
#
# .env.development still sets NEXT_PUBLIC_* because local development builds and
# runs in a single environment, where inlining is harmless.
#
# The one exception below is a build-mode switch, not an environment value, so
# baking it in is correct. It must be defined rather than merely absent: Next
# only substitutes NEXT_PUBLIC_* names that exist at build time, and the minifier
# can only drop the code guarded by this flag -- along with the NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# reads inside it -- when the flag folds to a literal false.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_INLINED_CONFIG=false
